WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:01.340
I wanna live - Scene Breakdown

00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:03.800
What do ALL iconic scenes - have in common?

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:09.030
And I’m not limiting this question just
to One Piece or even Anime and Manga.

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:15.230
Seriously, what unites any iconic scene that
you love, no matter if it’s in a book, a

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:18.140
movie, an anime or even a photograph?

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:23.539
- The most fundamental answer to this question,
that I personally came up with, is that they

00:00:23.539 --> 00:00:29.650
all manage to create real - heart-felt emotion
- and my reasoning for this answer is this:

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:35.829
A scene can be iconic for a variety of reasons,
right? - because it’s incredibly funny,

00:00:35.829 --> 00:00:40.309
sad, epic, horrifying, heartwarming - you
name it.

00:00:40.309 --> 00:00:46.220
But, in the end, as diverse as these moments
might seem on the surface, on the most fundamental

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:50.320
level, stories are all about making us FELL
something.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:55.500
We love loosing ourselves in fictional worlds
and epic adventures, because it allows us

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:59.560
to experience moments, we could never have
in real life.

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:04.949
However, as any aspiring writer will know,
actually creating authentic and impactful

00:01:04.949 --> 00:01:08.460
emotions in a scene - is anything but easy.

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:13.770
The fact that Oda has managed to create so
many of these moments, really speaks for the

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:18.869
understanding he has for his craft and frankly,
without it, his story would probably never

00:01:18.869 --> 00:01:21.700
have been able to run for as long as it has.

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:26.990
As we will explore more and more throughout
this series of videos, the most iconic moments

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:32.679
in One Piece all do an exceptional job at
making us feel a certain way and many can

00:01:32.679 --> 00:01:35.840
undoubtably be described as tear-jerkers.

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:40.649
What I find truly fascinating about this,
and I think you might as well, is that there

00:01:40.649 --> 00:01:45.850
is no one formula of how to achieve this,
and especially manga and anime have a number

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:48.149
of unique tools to achieve this.

00:01:48.149 --> 00:01:52.869
Therefore, the scene we will be breaking down
today, will be an absolute masterclass in

00:01:52.869 --> 00:01:57.179
how to create a strong emotional response
in your audience.

00:01:57.179 --> 00:02:02.969
It is one of THE highlights of the water7
- Ennis lobby arc, coincidentally my favourite

00:02:02.969 --> 00:02:05.240
arc in the entire story so far.

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:09.752
I think you know what moment I’m talking
about - mainly cause it’s the title of this

00:02:09.752 --> 00:02:19.849
video, fair enough - but I think even without
it you would probably have guessed which one

00:02:19.849 --> 00:02:20.849
I’m talking about.

00:02:20.849 --> 00:02:22.379
Wahh Goosebumps.

00:02:22.379 --> 00:02:27.560
I’m really happy you guys seem to enjoy
this new series as much as I do, cause I’m

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:32.500
frankly having a real blast re-reading and
re-watching these scenes, and at risk of sounding

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:38.530
a bit cocky, it’s also so much fun building
a new format from scratch that isn’t out

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:39.530
there yet.

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:44.310
So, thanks for sticking with me here and thanks
for sharing all your amazing ideas and thoughts

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:45.430
with me!

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:50.739
Okay but now enough sweet talk I think, it’s
time to go through some feels again.

00:02:50.739 --> 00:02:55.280
So grab yourself a cup of coffee and some
tissues and let’s get into this beauty of

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:56.609
a scene.

00:02:56.609 --> 00:03:00.999
Before we get into the analysis part, I will
do a quick recap, so if you wanna skip that,

00:03:00.999 --> 00:03:03.750
you can simply jump to this time code here.

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:11.439
The corresponding chapters are 391 and 399
and for the anime it’s episode 278, in case

00:03:11.439 --> 00:03:14.150
you wanna read or watch along.

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:17.470
The scene takes place at the height of the
Ennis Lobby arc.

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:21.700
The straw hats have fought their way to the
tower of justice and start their legendary

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:26.750
walk to Ennis Lobby, where they face Robin
and the members of CP9.

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:31.359
Robin is shocked to see them there and tells
them that she won’t return to them and that

00:03:31.359 --> 00:03:35.590
she wants to die, all to protect her newly
found friends from the wrath of the world

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:37.370
government.

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:42.249
This is followed by Robin’s flashback and
the events of Ohara, where we truly get to

00:03:42.249 --> 00:03:46.600
know Robin and her true personality and dreams
for the very first time.

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:51.840
Re-living her tragic coming of age story and
all the hate, rejection and betrayal she had

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:56.341
to endure, she fears that she will bring nothing
but unfortunate upon those around her, even

00:03:56.341 --> 00:03:59.610
though she clearly loves the straw hats at
this point.

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:05.400
And, what she fears the most, even more than
death, is to be abandoned and betrayed once

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:10.069
again, just as crocodile and many others had
done to her before.

00:04:10.069 --> 00:04:13.959
At this point she has truly given up on life.

00:04:13.959 --> 00:04:18.380
She once again warns Spandam about the horrors
of the Buster call, who carelessly threatens

00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:20.099
to use it on the island.

00:04:20.099 --> 00:04:25.520
He asks Robin, how anybody could ever NOT
see her as a burden, when her enemy is the

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:31.000
world government itself, pointing at the flag
on top of the tower of justice, asking Luffy

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:35.290
whether he truly understands WHO he is facing
here.

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:41.220
Luffy however coldly replies that he understands
very well who Robin’s enemies are - and

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:47.039
without so much as a hint of uncertainty,
he orders Usopp to shoot down the World Government’s

00:04:47.039 --> 00:04:49.980
flag towering over the island.

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:56.169
Usopp steps forward and burns down the flag,
while all of the straw hats watch with stoic

00:04:56.169 --> 00:04:57.430
faces.

00:04:57.430 --> 00:05:02.280
With this, the straw hats have now officially
declared war on the world, and thus taken

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:05.539
away Robin’s reason for protecting and rejecting
them.

00:05:05.539 --> 00:05:10.160
Then, Luffy tells Robin to say that she wants
to live.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:14.350
Recalling her tragic past, Saul’s final
words to her that she will surely find Nakama

00:05:14.350 --> 00:05:20.669
one day and finally Usopp asking her to trust
in Luffy, she finally breaks free of her mental

00:05:20.669 --> 00:05:30.220
prison and shouts her dream.

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:34.760
After this, Franky declares his love for the
straw hats as well and destroys the plans

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:36.160
for the Pluton.

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:42.020
Then the bridge lowers and the straw hats
as well as CP9 prepare for battle.

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:46.110
Okay, so what makes this scene so special?

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:50.730
How is Oda able to create such an intense
amount of emotional response with this moment

00:05:50.730 --> 00:05:51.730
here.

00:05:51.730 --> 00:05:55.099
There are a couple of things I want to get
into here, but the most fundamental element

00:05:55.099 --> 00:05:59.050
I believe is emotional contrasting.

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:04.770
What makes Robin’s words SO powerful, is
not the words themselves, but the chain of

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:08.380
emotional sequences leading up to that moment.

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:12.550
At the outset of Ennis Lobby, we have grown
to more or less accept Robin as a part of

00:06:12.550 --> 00:06:13.580
the crew.

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:18.069
She has traveled with the straw hats to the
sky islands and established a nice presence

00:06:18.069 --> 00:06:19.069
on the ship.

00:06:19.069 --> 00:06:24.349
However, her character is still shrouded in
much mystery and neither we the reader, nor

00:06:24.349 --> 00:06:29.479
the crew really knows whether it’s okay
to fully trust her as an ally yet.

00:06:29.479 --> 00:06:35.580
Her abduction by the CP9 is kept purposefully
ambiguous by Oda, where we only slowly learn

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:39.259
that something is happening against Robin’s
will here.

00:06:39.259 --> 00:06:44.300
Luffy is the only one that truly understands
her right from the start.

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:49.569
His unique ability to sense a person’s true
character and their intentions might even

00:06:49.569 --> 00:06:53.470
have been the reason he saved her form the
tomb in Alabasta in the first place.

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:57.940
He must have been aware right from the start
of all the pain and sorrow that Robin had

00:06:57.940 --> 00:07:02.460
been carrying in her heart and knew that she
was looking for a place that she belonged.

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:08.099
Thus, he immediately takes his crew and follows
her to Ennis lobby to take her back, knowing

00:07:08.099 --> 00:07:12.229
that this is what she really wants.

00:07:12.229 --> 00:07:16.990
Even if we don’t know about Luffy’s ability
at this point, seeing our main character this

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:22.830
invested and determined, we can’t help but
become involved into Robin’s rescue as well.

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:27.080
This is followed by the crew’s raid on the
island and their fight against time before

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:31.700
Robin is shipped away through the gates of
justice, where she will forever be out of

00:07:31.700 --> 00:07:33.199
reach.

00:07:33.199 --> 00:07:38.479
This builds enormous urgency and raises the
stakes for every single moment during the

00:07:38.479 --> 00:07:43.629
arc, leaving us on the edges of our seats
whether or not Luffy will make it in time.

00:07:43.629 --> 00:07:48.669
At the same time, seeing his newly gained
abilities with Gear 2 gives us hope that this

00:07:48.669 --> 00:07:51.689
is actually a battle that might be won.

00:07:51.689 --> 00:07:56.719
The epic walk to Ennis lobby and the determination
of the crew to get their Nakama back is a

00:07:56.719 --> 00:07:59.370
pure firework of euphoric shivers.

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:04.280
However, this is immediately countered by
Robin’s sudden anger and her declaration

00:08:04.280 --> 00:08:05.940
that she wants to die.

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:12.270
We can kinda tell that there is more going
on here, that she does indeed want to be saved,

00:08:12.270 --> 00:08:15.289
but why in the world does she behave this
way?

00:08:15.289 --> 00:08:20.100
This is when we finally get the flashback
into her past, the harsh and lonely childhood

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:25.030
she had, how she lost the only place that
ever accepted her and how she had been on

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:30.500
the run from the world at large for her entire
life having no-one to turn to.

00:08:30.500 --> 00:08:36.170
Confronted with, in my opinion, the most tragic
backstory of any straw hat, we get punched

00:08:36.170 --> 00:08:42.560
in the gut with a wave of sadness, pity and
dawning comprehension of who Robin truly is

00:08:42.560 --> 00:08:43.640
as a person.

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:48.840
Suddenly, we understand her character fully
and it makes the events until now and the

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:54.790
current situation just the more impactful
and engaging.

00:08:54.790 --> 00:09:02.380
- Now, me stopping the clip right at this
moment, might have made you twitch a little,

00:09:02.380 --> 00:09:07.970
or maybe you even felt annoyed, wanting to
see what happens next - how Robin reacts to

00:09:07.970 --> 00:09:09.040
this, even though you already know what will
happen.

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:13.390
That is the type of engagement you want to
reach as a writer when it comes to capturing

00:09:13.390 --> 00:09:14.660
your audience.

00:09:14.660 --> 00:09:20.790
This moment is CHARGED with anticipation and
emotion and is what makes it so memorable.

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:26.020
You can’t help but see what happens next.

00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:31.790
This of course makes Robins words the ultimate
catharsis after building up the tension towards

00:09:31.790 --> 00:09:36.400
this scene for countless chapters, while at
the same time setting the mood for the second

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:40.270
half of the arc and the fights that follow.

00:09:40.270 --> 00:09:46.280
We are 110% involved in this mission to save
Robin now and want to see our heroes succeed

00:09:46.280 --> 00:09:49.590
against an amazing cast of antagonists.

00:09:49.590 --> 00:09:55.000
Now, moving on to the scene itself, one of
the things that stood out to me the most here,

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:58.340
was the crazy amount of symbolism it contained.

00:09:58.340 --> 00:10:02.950
In general, Oda loves filling his story with
symbols and references.

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:08.270
Some are small and arc-specific, while others
span the entirety of the story.

00:10:08.270 --> 00:10:13.660
There are some rather obvious symbols here,
like the walk to the tower, which directly

00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:18.460
references the walk to along park or Usopp
shooting down the flag, which is generally

00:10:18.460 --> 00:10:21.850
known to be a declaration of war throughout
history.

00:10:21.850 --> 00:10:26.320
But the flag itself, ALSO symbolises a lot
here.

00:10:26.320 --> 00:10:30.210
The world government as a whole and the political
system behind it.

00:10:30.210 --> 00:10:35.730
It represents the power of the world and the
weight it has towering over the entire island

00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:38.790
- and more specifically over Robin.

00:10:38.790 --> 00:10:43.880
Thus, burning it down does not only mean the
straw hats declaring war on the world, but

00:10:43.880 --> 00:10:49.390
it also symbolises the influence that the
government had on Robin vanishing by burning

00:10:49.390 --> 00:10:52.140
her doubts and fears to ashes.

00:10:52.140 --> 00:10:57.810
The fire itself meanwhile is therefore a literal
light in the darkness for her, as she finally

00:10:57.810 --> 00:11:03.680
accepts and understands that Luffy and the
crew truly have come solely for her sake and

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:05.880
with no ulterior motives.

00:11:05.880 --> 00:11:12.320
She is truly able to trust someone again for
the first time since loosing her home.

00:11:12.320 --> 00:11:17.660
The anime does an especially wonderful job
here at visualising this, showing her leaving

00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:21.420
behind her darkness and going into the light.

00:11:21.420 --> 00:11:25.650
Fantastic visual symbolism here where she
finally is able to join her friends with all

00:11:25.650 --> 00:11:27.370
she is.

00:11:27.370 --> 00:11:33.270
This transition also includes another symbol
of the Water 7 and Ennis Lobby arc over all:

00:11:33.270 --> 00:11:34.270
Masks.

00:11:34.270 --> 00:11:39.520
What they represent, is pretending to be someone
you are not and literally putting on a false

00:11:39.520 --> 00:11:40.520
face.

00:11:40.520 --> 00:11:45.680
We can see this with Franky, the CP9 and of
course Usopp.

00:11:45.680 --> 00:11:51.120
But Robin in many ways also is putting on
a mask throughout the arc, trying to push

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:53.540
Luffy and the others away.

00:11:53.540 --> 00:11:59.830
In this scene, Luffy breaks that mask and
she is able to show her true face and true

00:11:59.830 --> 00:12:03.910
intentions, finally being the person she really
is.

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:10.050
Thus the ‘I want to live’ moment stands
in direct contrast to the ‘I want to die’

00:12:10.050 --> 00:12:15.310
moment just a little earlier, hammering home
the impact the straw hats’ actions and words

00:12:15.310 --> 00:12:18.430
have had on her in this short amount of time.

00:12:18.430 --> 00:12:23.520
She has accepted that she is actually worth
something and that she is worth to be cared

00:12:23.520 --> 00:12:25.910
for and rescued by her friends.

00:12:25.910 --> 00:12:31.450
Meanwhile, the golden snail held by Spandam
and the destructive Buster Call it can summon

00:12:31.450 --> 00:12:36.510
symbolise Robin’s traumatic childhood and
all her suffering that she had to go through

00:12:36.510 --> 00:12:38.610
by having to experience it.

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:44.480
And finally, I think it’s fair to say that
the tower of justice itself also is a symbol.

00:12:44.480 --> 00:12:49.940
The name seems to be quite ironic at first,
since it seems to show the hypocrisy and twisted

00:12:49.940 --> 00:12:52.260
sense of justice of the world government.

00:12:52.260 --> 00:12:57.720
However, with Oda putting in another twist
here, at the end of the arc, the tower of

00:12:57.720 --> 00:13:03.430
justice has actually lived up to its name,
as Robin truly does get what she deserves:

00:13:03.430 --> 00:13:08.660
Freedom, a new family that loves her and a
place that she belongs.

00:13:08.660 --> 00:13:13.770
I would say that it’s a bit cheesy, but
that stuff is just so damn powerful.

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:15.530
Damn you Oda.

00:13:15.530 --> 00:13:21.250
Now, how is the character’s body language
&amp; the dialog in this scene implemented?

00:13:21.250 --> 00:13:25.870
Well I think the portrayal of Robin’s emotion
speaks for itself.

00:13:25.870 --> 00:13:31.350
The facial expressions and the conflict within
her are wonderfully drawn by Oda and the anime

00:13:31.350 --> 00:13:35.030
also does a great job at capturing her emotional
transformation.

00:13:35.030 --> 00:13:39.750
The way she is finally able to cry and let
out all the emotions that she had suppressed

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:43.770
for so long are simply overwhelming to see.

00:13:43.770 --> 00:13:49.050
And beside that, I think the scene manages
to bring out her inner dialog in a very believable

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:54.430
and convincing way, giving us some crucial
insight into her inner world.

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:58.970
Next to Robin, I think the scene also has
some wonderful language for the other straw

00:13:58.970 --> 00:14:00.170
hats.

00:14:00.170 --> 00:14:05.070
Of course there is Luffy, who’s intense
and emotion-filled speech towards Robin is

00:14:05.070 --> 00:14:09.520
one of the most important moments for his
character arc in my opinion, giving us one

00:14:09.520 --> 00:14:14.490
of these occasional moments where Luffy’s
true capabilities as a leader come clearly

00:14:14.490 --> 00:14:16.040
to light.

00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:19.180
And what about the other straw hats?

00:14:19.180 --> 00:14:26.290
I think I have rarely seen a manga or anime
do such a fantastic job with silence as in

00:14:26.290 --> 00:14:28.230
this scene.

00:14:28.230 --> 00:14:30.680
Because none of the straw hats says - anything.

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:36.510
They don’t address Robin, they don’t cry
out in shock when Luffy tells Usopp to shoot

00:14:36.510 --> 00:14:43.050
down the flag, they don’t show fear or anger
- or really Any sign of emotional effect this

00:14:43.050 --> 00:14:46.390
moment could or actually should have on them.

00:14:46.390 --> 00:14:52.500
No, they decide to simply stand there next
to Luffy, side by side with a stoic and determined

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:58.100
look on their face, radiating nothing but
pure confidence and trust in their captain

00:14:58.100 --> 00:15:01.360
and dedication to get their friend back.

00:15:01.360 --> 00:15:07.100
Sadly, show-don’t-tell is an important skill
in storytelling that somehow is heavily underused

00:15:07.100 --> 00:15:12.620
in Anime and Manga and especially Shounen,
where often everything is explained so everyone

00:15:12.620 --> 00:15:15.780
in the audience can get it.

00:15:15.780 --> 00:15:21.830
But I think this is a perfect example, how
powerful silence can be and simply letting

00:15:21.830 --> 00:15:24.110
the visual speak for itself.

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:31.370
Just watch.

00:15:31.370 --> 00:15:33.410
THIS - is what gives me goosebumps.

00:15:33.410 --> 00:15:38.580
I don’t need everyone in the crew to say
out loud that they want to save Robin.

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:42.080
This is the way to do it and to get me on
board with this scene.

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:46.450
Finally, next to Robin I think it’s also
worth mentioning the change we see in some

00:15:46.450 --> 00:15:51.850
other characters in this moment.

00:15:51.850 --> 00:15:58.170
Franky for instance finally completely changes
from antagonist to ally in this moment, being

00:15:58.170 --> 00:16:03.570
deeply moved and showing his true colors as
well as his affection for the straw hats here.

00:16:03.570 --> 00:16:08.570
This results in him destroying the plans of
Pluton and fully following into the steps

00:16:08.570 --> 00:16:13.290
of his beloved master Tom, who worked for
the former pirate king Roger during his time.

00:16:13.290 --> 00:16:15.990
A quite overlooked moment I believe.

00:16:15.990 --> 00:16:22.730
Spandam of course changes from a sense of
superiority and arrogance to fear and panic

00:16:22.730 --> 00:16:27.620
once the flag is taken down and while his
character might be annoying beyond help, it

00:16:27.620 --> 00:16:32.730
does a wonderful job at getting us fired up
for his defeat and also shaping Lucci to be

00:16:32.730 --> 00:16:36.770
the way cooler and more threatening antagonist
of this arc.

00:16:36.770 --> 00:16:42.890
And speaking of Lucci, his face in this scene
goes from indifferent and annoyed to full

00:16:42.890 --> 00:16:48.290
ecstasy and blood thirst, something that hypes
up the second half of the arc and his later

00:16:48.290 --> 00:16:50.470
encounter with Luffy even more.

00:16:50.470 --> 00:16:56.670
The scene is also heavily accented by a great
use of sound effects and music.

00:16:56.670 --> 00:17:01.940
The flag of the world government flying heavily
in the wind, the silence as Usopp shoots down

00:17:01.940 --> 00:17:06.890
the flag, the sound of the flames mixing in
with Robins tears as well as the music when

00:17:06.890 --> 00:17:12.949
Robin finally breaks free are all greatly
chosen and do the scene justice I think.

00:17:12.949 --> 00:17:18.630
Also, special probs to Luffy’s and Robin’s
voice actors, both of which do a wonderful

00:17:18.630 --> 00:17:23.180
job here carrying the heavy emotions in this
scene with their performance.

00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:27.419
One thing I think is not optimal though is
Spandam’s VA.

00:17:27.419 --> 00:17:34.320
I’m not exactly sure what it is, but I think
there was more potential here to portray him

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:39.370
in a more unpredictable and threatening way,
compared to the mostly comic voice we got

00:17:39.370 --> 00:17:40.370
for him in the end.

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:42.800
Just a side note.

00:17:42.800 --> 00:17:46.409
The last thing I want to look at is the framing
in this scene.

00:17:46.409 --> 00:17:51.799
In general, Ennis Lobby has great framing
and camera movement all over.

00:17:51.799 --> 00:17:54.750
However there are some things that stood out
to me.

00:17:54.750 --> 00:18:00.669
The scene opens up with a wide shot of Ennis
lobby showing the literal and metaphorical

00:18:00.669 --> 00:18:05.200
chasm between Robin and the crew, isolating
her from her friends.

00:18:05.200 --> 00:18:10.140
I think this is quite purposefully done here
and I simply love the effect it has on the

00:18:10.140 --> 00:18:11.539
reader.

00:18:11.539 --> 00:18:17.390
In general of course, the entire island’s
theme is focused around these monstrous structures

00:18:17.390 --> 00:18:22.289
there, showing the power of the world government
and giving the stage an epic feel.

00:18:22.289 --> 00:18:27.590
Thus, when showing Ennis lobby even smaller
before the enormous gates of justice with

00:18:27.590 --> 00:18:32.350
the world government icon on it and when robin
says, that no-one has allowed her to follow

00:18:32.350 --> 00:18:39.240
her own dreams, the giant iron gates tower
threateningly over the entire moment.

00:18:39.240 --> 00:18:44.029
The same goes for the government flag that
Spandam points up to, overlooking the entire

00:18:44.029 --> 00:18:46.990
scene as a sort of protective force.

00:18:46.990 --> 00:18:52.190
And I also am a sucker for this panel here,
where the straw hats stand at the edge of

00:18:52.190 --> 00:18:56.750
the abyss - absolutely fearless - staring
down the CP9.

00:18:56.750 --> 00:19:02.590
And the way that the CP9 members mirror that
pose in just the same way, creates a fantastic

00:19:02.590 --> 00:19:06.440
sense of balanced opposition and contrast.

00:19:06.440 --> 00:19:12.320
Not only does it foreshadow the battle, but
also the similarity between both groups, with

00:19:12.320 --> 00:19:18.100
the CP9 being a “more evil” version of
the straw hats.

00:19:18.100 --> 00:19:23.539
And last but not least, Luffy’s and Robin’s
matching close up shots, with Robin answering

00:19:23.539 --> 00:19:27.330
her captains call and fully becoming part
of his crew - Beautiful.

00:19:27.330 --> 00:19:31.290
So, what is the overall purpose of this scene?

00:19:31.290 --> 00:19:34.580
And how does it fit into the context of the
story?

00:19:34.580 --> 00:19:39.730
Of course Ennis Lobby as an arc overall plays
a major roles in building the world and driving

00:19:39.730 --> 00:19:46.110
the story forward, but focusing on just this
one scene here, I think, that if there is

00:19:46.110 --> 00:19:51.500
one thing in particular it achieves above
all else is that it gives major development

00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:57.169
to four of the straw hats: Robin, Luffy, Usopp
and Franky.

00:19:57.169 --> 00:20:02.620
Let’s look at this list from last to first
- you know so we have the more dramatic ending

00:20:02.620 --> 00:20:05.029
for this video - storytelling.

00:20:05.029 --> 00:20:07.559
So let’s start with Franky.

00:20:07.559 --> 00:20:12.610
There is not too much focus on his character
in this sequence and yet, in retrospect it

00:20:12.610 --> 00:20:18.580
is fairly obvious that Oda is already shaping
Franky to become a straw hat here.

00:20:18.580 --> 00:20:23.470
Witnessing this incredibly emotional and powerful
moment between the straw hats serves as a

00:20:23.470 --> 00:20:28.870
sort of breaking point for him, where he also
is finally able to drop his mask and show

00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:34.030
his emotional and kind-hearted side, already
declaring his love for the crew.

00:20:34.030 --> 00:20:39.340
By burning the plans of the pluton before
Spandam’s and the CP9’s eyes, he mimics

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:44.480
Luffy’s declaration of war on the government
and thus qualifies himself to join them at

00:20:44.480 --> 00:20:46.040
the end of the arc.

00:20:46.040 --> 00:20:50.690
In general, I believe that Franky’s arc
here on Ennis Lobby is quite underrated, which

00:20:50.690 --> 00:20:55.470
is to be expected when it’s overshadowed
by Robin’s incredible story line.

00:20:55.470 --> 00:21:00.820
But nonetheless, I think it’s important
to appreciate how subtly Oda turns his character

00:21:00.820 --> 00:21:02.149
around in this moment.

00:21:02.149 --> 00:21:05.429
Then of course we have - Usopp.

00:21:05.429 --> 00:21:10.429
The entirety of Ennis Lobby serves as Usopp’s
redemption arc after defying Luffy and leaving

00:21:10.429 --> 00:21:12.539
the crew on Water 7.

00:21:12.539 --> 00:21:16.111
While there are many moments, that are important
to his re-establishment as a member of the

00:21:16.111 --> 00:21:21.679
straw hats, like on the sea train with Robin
or later at the port, this scene here, where

00:21:21.679 --> 00:21:26.850
he without hesitation follows Luffy’s orders
to declare war on the world, might be the

00:21:26.850 --> 00:21:30.000
most important for him in terms of symbolism
and impact.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:36.499
He shows us that he now fully accepts Luffy
as his captain and makes another step to becoming

00:21:36.499 --> 00:21:38.909
a brave warrior of the sea.

00:21:38.909 --> 00:21:44.360
And while the flag scene is definitely anything
BUT underrated, the role Usopp plays in it

00:21:44.360 --> 00:21:46.159
definitely is, I believe.

00:21:46.159 --> 00:21:49.970
Next, we of course have to talk about Luffy.

00:21:49.970 --> 00:21:55.490
As mentioned before, his speech here at the
tower of justice is one of the best moments

00:21:55.490 --> 00:21:57.840
for his role as captain of the crew.

00:21:57.840 --> 00:22:02.659
Oftentimes, Luffy shows his thoughts and emotions
through actions and fighting.

00:22:02.659 --> 00:22:08.330
Here however, he actually finds exactly the
right words one would expect from a captain

00:22:08.330 --> 00:22:13.480
and future pirate king, and it’s one of
the moments I always remind people off, whenever

00:22:13.480 --> 00:22:16.520
they say that Luffy is not a good leader.

00:22:16.520 --> 00:22:21.519
The point is, that Luffy is BECOMING a good
leader and it’s moments like these that

00:22:21.519 --> 00:22:23.340
show this growth.

00:22:23.340 --> 00:22:29.050
When it counts Luffy can loose his naivety
and easy-going nature and become serious.

00:22:29.050 --> 00:22:33.830
And it’s moments like this one here or the
one where he gives Nami his hat, where I think

00:22:33.830 --> 00:22:38.009
most of us gain the most respect for Luffy
as a main character.

00:22:38.009 --> 00:22:40.879
And that brings us back to Robin.

00:22:40.879 --> 00:22:45.320
The way Oda shows her moment of liberation
in this scene and how he builds up all that

00:22:45.320 --> 00:22:50.019
emotion and suspense for her character is
simply one of my favourite moments in One

00:22:50.019 --> 00:22:55.580
Piece and the reason that this video easily
deserves a spot in this series of videos.

00:22:55.580 --> 00:23:00.549
Robin in this moment becomes a full-fledged
straw hat and her development from Alabasta

00:23:00.549 --> 00:23:09.669
- 
until this moment is one of my favourite character

00:23:09.669 --> 00:23:12.299
arcs of all time.

00:23:12.299 --> 00:23:17.389
Robin breaking out of her depression and seeing
how Saul’s words have come full circle is

00:23:17.389 --> 00:23:28.330
a powerful moment to witness.She 
now finally has found a place that she belongs

00:23:28.330 --> 00:23:33.389
to after loosing the scholars on Ohara and
for the first time she is able to rely fully

00:23:33.389 --> 00:23:35.570
on someone else.

00:23:35.570 --> 00:23:40.029
In this moment, Robin is prepared to live
life to its fullest.

00:23:40.029 --> 00:23:45.230
Now, while Luffy’s speech in this scene
is incredibly touching and powerful, coming

00:23:45.230 --> 00:23:49.769
from the hero of our story, I think it is
quite surprising that another iconic moment

00:23:49.769 --> 00:23:52.289
in One Piece is another speech.

00:23:52.289 --> 00:23:57.279
However, it doesn’t come from Luffy or any
other of our heroes, but from none other than

00:23:57.279 --> 00:24:01.419
the main villain of the story: Blackbeard’s
speech on Gaia.

00:24:01.419 --> 00:24:07.450
We will discuss this epic moment in the next
video, so stay tuned for that.

00:24:07.450 --> 00:24:08.559
Thanks guys, peace.

